From 223800fbdd90e1d835d90e133a30340bdd51dee8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 04:19:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 53/56] signet: signets whose blocks only an ML-DSA-44 key
 signs (-signetpqchallenge)

-signetpqchallenge=<pubkey> sets the challenge to the P2MR output of an
ML-DSA-44 key: its OP_CHECKMLDSA44 leaf next to a leaf that can only fail,
both at depth one (doc/signet-pqchallenge.md). The challenge is derived from
the key rather than taken as given, because a single-leaf P2MR output is spent
without running its leaf.

On such a signet the solution is checked with the P2MR and OP_CHECKMLDSA44
script rules, the witness commitment output must be exactly OP_RETURN, the
commitment and the solution push in its shortest encoding, and OP_CHECKMLDSA44
is active in transactions from height 1. Nodes that only get the same
challenge through -signetchallenge check solutions with the old flags, under
which a P2MR program is an unknown witness version: every node of such a
network needs the option.
